# Build outputs of gamecube/recomp/sr/build_image.sh, and the disc-derived inputs it
# needs. NOT tracked, for three separate reasons — each of which has bitten this repo:
#
# 1. SIZE + LFS + GITHUB PAGES. The repo's .gitattributes routes `*.wasm` and `*.bin`
#    through Git LFS, and **GitHub Pages does not resolve LFS pointers** — it serves the
#    133-byte pointer file as if it were the asset. That is exactly how the Dreamcast
#    Track3 disc parts shipped broken on day one (commit ffa15b3, "Pages served pointers,
#    the game crashed at boot"). sab_image.wasm is ~44 MB; putting it through LFS would
#    reproduce that failure, and putting it in git directly would add 44 MB per rebuild.
#
# 2. REGENERABLE IN ONE COMMAND, from tracked sources:
#       bash gamecube/recomp/sr/build_image.sh "gamecube/roms/Sonic Adventure 2 - Battle (USA).iso"
#    sr_gen.c (33 MB) and sr_dispatch.c are sr.py output, not hand-written code. Tracking
#    generated C would make every translator change a 33 MB diff nobody can review.
#
# 3. sab_main.dol AND sab_fst.bin ARE DISC CONTENT — the executable and the file system
#    table lifted out of the retail ISO, which .gitignore:73 already excludes.
#
# What IS tracked here: sr_image_worker.js, sr_image_boot.html and this file. The build
# script, the host layer (../sr/sr_image.c) and the probe (../../tools/sr_image_probe.mjs)
# live outside this directory and are tracked there.
sab_image.mjs
sab_image.wasm
sab_main.dol
sab_fst.bin
sr_gen.c
sr_dispatch.c
skiplist.json
